GRAPH <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/blob/main/packages/starlayer/starlayer/graph/query/algebra_translator_patches.py> {
    ns63:algebra_translator_patches.py dcterms:identifier "starlayer.graph.query.algebra_translator_patches" ;
        a ns2:Module ;
        rdfs:comment """Targeted compatibility shims for confirmed bugs in plain rdflib's own
``_AlgebraTranslator``/``translateAlgebra`` (``rdflib.plugins.sparql.algebra``)
— algebra-tree-back-to-SPARQL-text serialization, not evaluation. See
``docs/upstream-issues/rdflib-upstream-issues.md`` issues 3, 4, and 6 for the full write-up
of each, including standalone plain-rdflib reproductions.

None of these bugs is in a code path *this repo itself* exercises directly
today — starlayer.graph never calls ``translateAlgebra``/``_AlgebraTranslator``
anywhere in its own pipeline. They surfaced in the downstream
``starlayer.sparql`` project, which *does* use ``_AlgebraTranslator``
directly (subclassing it in its own ``serialize12.py``); issues 3 and 6
already have independent workarounds there (issue 7's empty-``PV`` fix does
not — that project's own ``Project`` handling is about a different,
CONSTRUCT-specific empty-``PV`` case, not this one). Patching here too is
worthwhile, matching ``operator_patches.py``'s own stated rationale: any
*other* current or future consumer of this package that calls
``translateAlgebra``/``_AlgebraTranslator`` directly (not through that
specific downstream subclass) gets correct behavior for free, rather than
silently inheriting these bugs — and this ``translateAlgebra``-based
pipeline (parse SPARQL 1.2 → this project's own RDF algebra representation
→ regeneration → execution) is intended to become the path *every* SPARQL
query through starlayer.graph goes through, not just this one downstream
project's own test suite, which is why these are fixed here rather than
only in that one consumer's own workaround.

Same idempotent apply-once pattern as ``operator_patches.py``: a
module-level ``_xxx_patch_status: bool | None`` flag plus a marker attribute
on the patched callable, so repeated calls are safe no-ops. Unlike
``operator_patches.py``'s ``Comp.setEvalFn`` technique (that file patches
pyparsing grammar nodes), this patches a plain Python method on
``_AlgebraTranslator`` directly: the original bound method is captured once,
and the replacement delegates to it for every node type except the two
specific ``node.name`` values these two bugs live in - so any future rdflib
fix, or any other branch's behavior, passes through completely unaffected.""" ;
        rdfs:label "algebra_translator_patches" ;
        ns2:declares ns64:patch_algebra_translator_bugs, ns64:_is_aggregate_result_var ;
        ns2:filePath "packages/starlayer/starlayer/graph/query/algebra_translator_patches.py" ;
        ns2:importsModule ns5:__future__, ns5:re, ns5:rdflib.plugins.sparql.parserutils, ns5:rdflib.plugins.sparql.algebra, ns5:rdflib .

    ns64:_is_aggregate_result_var dcterms:identifier "starlayer.graph.query.algebra_translator_patches._is_aggregate_result_var" ;
        a ns2:Function ;
        rdfs:label "_is_aggregate_result_var" ;
        ns2:filePath "packages/starlayer/starlayer/graph/query/algebra_translator_patches.py" ;
        ns2:hasParameter ns64:_is_aggregate_result_var.param.expr ;
        ns2:hasReturnValue ns64:_is_aggregate_result_var.returns ;
        ns2:isPrivate true ;
        ns2:lineEnd 60 ;
        ns2:lineStart 59 ;
        ns2:signature "def _is_aggregate_result_var(expr: object) -> bool" .

    ns64:_is_aggregate_result_var.param.expr a ns2:Parameter ;
        rdfs:label "expr" ;
        ns2:annotationText "object" ;
        ns2:hasType ns5:builtins.object ;
        ns2:parameterKind "positional" ;
        ns2:position 0 .

    ns64:_is_aggregate_result_var.returns a ns2:ReturnValue ;
        ns2:annotationText "bool" ;
        ns2:hasType ns5:builtins.bool .

    ns64:patch_algebra_translator_bugs dcterms:identifier "starlayer.graph.query.algebra_translator_patches.patch_algebra_translator_bugs" ;
        a ns2:Function ;
        rdfs:comment """Fix three confirmed rdflib bugs in ``_AlgebraTranslator.sparql_query_text``:

1. The ``"BGP"`` branch joins each triple's text with no separator
   between one triple's trailing ``"."`` and the next triple's leading
   term - so a triple ending in a blank-node object immediately
   followed by a triple whose subject is a blank node produces text
   rdflib's own SPARQL parser can't re-tokenize (``_:x._:x`` instead of
   ``_:x. _:x``). See ``docs/upstream-issues/rdflib-upstream-issues.md`` issue 3.

2. The ``"RelationalExpression"`` branch (``IN``/``NOT IN`` among other
   relational operators) guards its list-handling code with
   ``isinstance(list, type(node.other))`` - backwards from the intended
   ``isinstance(node.other, list)`` (never ``True`` for any value,
   since the class ``list`` is never an instance of itself), making the
   correct branch dead code - every multi-value ``IN``/``NOT IN`` falls
   through to ``self.convert_node_arg(node.other)``, which has no case
   for a bare list at all, and raises. See
   ``docs/upstream-issues/rdflib-upstream-issues.md`` issue 6.

3. The ``"Extend"`` branch (``BIND``/``SELECT (expr AS ?v)``) locates
   the variable it needs to wrap by searching the *already-accumulated
   output text* for a bare occurrence of ``var.n3()`` and replacing it
   in place with ``"(expr AS var)"`` - not idempotent-safe (the
   replacement text itself still contains that same substring) and not
   scoped per-branch, so when multiple sibling ``UNION`` branches each
   independently ``BIND`` the same projected variable name, a later
   branch's replacement matches *inside* an earlier branch's own,
   already-completed replacement instead of a fresh occurrence -
   producing invalid, arbitrarily-nested output. See
   ``docs/upstream-issues/rdflib-upstream-issues.md`` issue 4.

Idempotent and defensive, matching the established
``operator_patches.py`` idiom - returns ``False`` without raising if
rdflib's internals don't match what this shim expects.""" ;
        rdfs:label "patch_algebra_translator_bugs" ;
        ns2:filePath "packages/starlayer/starlayer/graph/query/algebra_translator_patches.py" ;
        ns2:hasReturnValue ns64:patch_algebra_translator_bugs.returns ;
        ns2:lineEnd 293 ;
        ns2:lineStart 63 ;
        ns2:signature "def patch_algebra_translator_bugs() -> bool" .

    ns64:patch_algebra_translator_bugs.returns a ns2:ReturnValue ;
        ns2:annotationText "bool" ;
        ns2:hasType ns5:builtins.bool .

    ns5:__future__ a ns2:ExternalModule .

    ns5:builtins.bool dcterms:identifier "builtins.bool" ;
        a ns2:ExternalType ;
        rdfs:label "bool" ;
        rdfs:subClassOf ns2:Type .

    ns5:builtins.object dcterms:identifier "builtins.object" ;
        a ns2:ExternalType ;
        rdfs:label "object" ;
        rdfs:subClassOf ns2:Type .

    ns5:rdflib a ns2:ExternalModule .

    ns5:rdflib.plugins.sparql.algebra a ns2:ExternalModule .

    ns5:rdflib.plugins.sparql.parserutils a ns2:ExternalModule .

    ns5:re a ns2:ExternalModule .
}

GRAPH <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/blob/main/packages/starlayer/starlayer/graph/query/builtin_error_patches.py> {
    ns63:builtin_error_patches.py dcterms:identifier "starlayer.graph.query.builtin_error_patches" ;
        a ns2:Module ;
        rdfs:comment """Compatibility shims for confirmed bugs in rdflib's SPARQL builtin functions
and expression error handling (``rdflib.plugins.sparql.operators``,
``aggregates``, ``algebra``). GitHub issue #76 (the second bug hunt); every
bug reproduces against plain ``rdflib.Graph().query()``. Write-ups with
standalone repros: ``docs/upstream-issues/rdflib-upstream-issues.md``.

What a SPARQL error means here: an expression that raises ``SPARQLError``
leaves a ``BIND``/projection target unbound, drops the row under ``FILTER``,
and is skipped by ``COALESCE`` (SPARQL 1.1/1.2 Query, 17.2). The bugs below
are cases where rdflib instead returned a wrong value or let a Python
exception (``AttributeError``, ``ValueError``, ``RecursionError``) abort the
whole query.

Same idempotent apply-once pattern as ``operator_patches.py``: a module-level
``_xxx_patch_status: bool | None`` flag plus a marker attribute on the patched
callable.""" ;
        rdfs:label "builtin_error_patches" ;
        ns2:declares ns65:patch_min_max_group_concat_terms_and_errors, ns65:patch_select_star_scope_and_describe_star, ns65:patch_strdt_requires_string_and_iri, ns65:_xpath_replacement, ns65:_replace_evalfn, ns65:patch_sparql_parser_keeps_tabs, ns65:_graph_of, ns65:_timezone_evalfn, ns65:patch_timezone_keeps_minutes, ns65:patch_rounding_of_special_doubles, ns65:patch_empty_values_clause, ns65:patch_relational_operators_follow_spec, ns65:_regex_evalfn, ns65:_expression_comp, ns65:patch_regex_and_replace_follow_xpath, ns65:normalise_directional_language, ns65:_substr_evalfn, ns65:patch_ill_typed_literals_are_errors, ns65:patch_substr_xpath_semantics, ns65:apply_all_builtin_error_patches, ns65:_make_rounding_evalfn, ns65:_in_evalfn, ns65:patch_sum_avg_errors_are_unbound, ns65:_compile_xpath_regex, ns65:_marked, ns65:xpath_replace, ns65:_value_equal, ns65:_is_marked, ns65:_ordering_class ;
        ns2:filePath "packages/starlayer/starlayer/graph/query/builtin_error_patches.py" ;
        ns2:importsModule ns5:__future__, ns5:rdflib, ns5:rdflib.namespace, ns5:types, ns5:rdflib.plugins.sparql.sparql, ns5:functools .

