    ns65:patch_ill_typed_literals_are_errors dcterms:identifier "starlayer.graph.query.builtin_error_patches.patch_ill_typed_literals_are_errors" ;
        a ns2:Function ;
        rdfs:comment """``numeric()`` returned the ``Literal`` itself for an ill-typed numeric
such as ``"abc"^^xsd:integer`` (rdflib's ``toPython`` falls back to the
literal), so ``+`` recursed until ``RecursionError`` and ``isNumeric``
answered true. ``datetime()``/``date()`` did the same for an ill-typed
``xsd:dateTime``, so ``DAY()``/``YEAR()`` and friends died with
``AttributeError``. SPARQL 1.1 Query 17.3: an ill-typed literal is a type
error. All of these now raise ``SPARQLError``.""" ;
        rdfs:label "patch_ill_typed_literals_are_errors" ;
        ns2:calls ns65:_is_marked ;
        ns2:filePath "packages/starlayer/starlayer/graph/query/builtin_error_patches.py" ;
        ns2:hasReturnValue ns65:patch_ill_typed_literals_are_errors.returns ;
        ns2:lineEnd 109 ;
        ns2:lineStart 58 ;
        ns2:signature "def patch_ill_typed_literals_are_errors() -> bool" .

    ns65:patch_ill_typed_literals_are_errors.returns a ns2:ReturnValue ;
        ns2:annotationText "bool" ;
        ns2:hasType ns5:builtins.bool .

    ns65:patch_min_max_group_concat_terms_and_errors dcterms:identifier "starlayer.graph.query.builtin_error_patches.patch_min_max_group_concat_terms_and_errors" ;
        a ns2:Function ;
        rdfs:comment """``MIN``/``MAX`` wrapped their result in ``Literal(value)``, so the minimum of IRIs came back as a plain string
literal and the minimum of triple terms as a literal holding the internal ``tt:`` hash IRI; ``GROUP_CONCAT`` and
``MIN``/``MAX`` also put the *error message* of a failed argument into the result (``GROUP_CONCAT(STR(?o))`` over a
triple term returned ``"... STR: a triple term has no string form"``, ``MAX(STR(?o))`` returned the message itself)
because ``_eval`` hands back a ``SPARQLError`` as a value. SPARQL 1.1 Query 18.5: ``Min``/``Max`` return a term of
the group (its own type), and an error in an aggregate argument makes the aggregate an error, so it is unbound
(GitHub issue #134). A triple term has no string form either, so ``GROUP_CONCAT(?o)`` over one is an error too.
A triple term sorts after every other kind of term (SPARQL 1.2 15.1 ORDER BY); the order among triple terms is not
defined by the spec and follows the content-addressed hash here.""" ;
        rdfs:label "patch_min_max_group_concat_terms_and_errors" ;
        ns2:calls ns65:_marked, ns65:_is_marked ;
        ns2:filePath "packages/starlayer/starlayer/graph/query/builtin_error_patches.py" ;
        ns2:hasReturnValue ns65:patch_min_max_group_concat_terms_and_errors.returns ;
        ns2:lineEnd 429 ;
        ns2:lineStart 340 ;
        ns2:signature "def patch_min_max_group_concat_terms_and_errors() -> bool" .

    ns65:patch_min_max_group_concat_terms_and_errors.returns a ns2:ReturnValue ;
        ns2:annotationText "bool" ;
        ns2:hasType ns5:builtins.bool .

    ns65:patch_regex_and_replace_follow_xpath dcterms:identifier "starlayer.graph.query.builtin_error_patches.patch_regex_and_replace_follow_xpath" ;
        a ns2:Function ;
        rdfs:comment """``REGEX``/``REPLACE`` with an invalid pattern raised ``re.error`` and aborted the query; ``fn:matches`` and
``fn:replace`` make it an error, which drops the row under ``FILTER`` and leaves a projection unbound. An invalid flag
(``REGEX(?x, "a", "z")``) was ignored. ``REPLACE`` also turned ``$0`` into a NUL character, accepted a pattern that
matches the zero-length string (error FORX0003), and passed its flags to ``re.sub`` as the ``count`` argument.""" ;
        rdfs:label "patch_regex_and_replace_follow_xpath" ;
        ns2:calls ns65:_is_marked, ns65:_expression_comp, ns65:_marked ;
        ns2:filePath "packages/starlayer/starlayer/graph/query/builtin_error_patches.py" ;
        ns2:hasReturnValue ns65:patch_regex_and_replace_follow_xpath.returns ;
        ns2:lineEnd 823 ;
        ns2:lineStart 799 ;
        ns2:signature "def patch_regex_and_replace_follow_xpath() -> bool" .

    ns65:patch_regex_and_replace_follow_xpath.returns a ns2:ReturnValue ;
        ns2:annotationText "bool" ;
        ns2:hasType ns5:builtins.bool .

    ns65:patch_relational_operators_follow_spec dcterms:identifier "starlayer.graph.query.builtin_error_patches.patch_relational_operators_follow_spec" ;
        a ns2:Function ;
        rdfs:comment """Wraps ``RelationalExpression`` and ``ConditionalAndExpression``.

* ``IN`` / ``NOT IN`` compared terms (``1 IN (1.0)`` was false) and
  swallowed an error in the list (``2 IN (1/0, 1)`` was false, not an
  error). Both are now chains of ``=`` tests (SPARQL 1.1 17.4.1.9).
* ``<``/``>``/``<=``/``>=`` between a numeric, a string, a boolean and a
  dateTime of different classes (``"x" > 1``) used rdflib's cross-type
  sort order and answered true; the operator mapping (17.3) defines no
  such comparison, so it is a type error.
* ``=`` / ``!=`` between directional literals that differ only in the case
  of the language tag compared the packed datatype IRI and answered false.
* ``&&`` returned an error for ``1/0 && false``; the truth table (17.2)
  gives false (error && false = false).""" ;
        rdfs:label "patch_relational_operators_follow_spec" ;
        ns2:calls ns65:_is_marked, ns65:_marked ;
        ns2:filePath "packages/starlayer/starlayer/graph/query/builtin_error_patches.py" ;
        ns2:hasReturnValue ns65:patch_relational_operators_follow_spec.returns ;
        ns2:lineEnd 599 ;
        ns2:lineStart 533 ;
        ns2:signature "def patch_relational_operators_follow_spec() -> bool" .

    ns65:patch_relational_operators_follow_spec.returns a ns2:ReturnValue ;
        ns2:annotationText "bool" ;
        ns2:hasType ns5:builtins.bool .

    ns65:patch_rounding_of_special_doubles dcterms:identifier "starlayer.graph.query.builtin_error_patches.patch_rounding_of_special_doubles" ;
        a ns2:Function ;
        rdfs:comment """``ROUND``/``FLOOR``/``CEIL`` converted the argument to a Python ``int``, which raised for ``NaN``, ``INF`` and
(``ROUND``) a very large double and aborted the query. fn:round, fn:floor and fn:ceiling give NaN and +/-INF back
unchanged, and a large double is already integral.""" ;
        rdfs:label "patch_rounding_of_special_doubles" ;
        ns2:calls ns65:_make_rounding_evalfn, ns65:_expression_comp, ns65:_is_marked ;
        ns2:filePath "packages/starlayer/starlayer/graph/query/builtin_error_patches.py" ;
        ns2:hasReturnValue ns65:patch_rounding_of_special_doubles.returns ;
        ns2:lineEnd 848 ;
        ns2:lineStart 826 ;
        ns2:signature "def patch_rounding_of_special_doubles() -> bool" .

