    ns26:patch_decimal_result_lexical_form dcterms:identifier "starlayer.graph.query.operator_patches.patch_decimal_result_lexical_form" ;
        a ns2:Function ;
        rdfs:comment """Fix a confirmed rdflib bug: ``Builtin_CEIL``/``Builtin_FLOOR``/
``Builtin_ROUND`` correctly preserve the argument's ``xsd:decimal``
datatype, but construct the result via ``Literal(int(...), datatype=...)``
- a raw Python ``int`` lexicalizes as e.g. ``"4"``, not the canonical
decimal form ``"4.0"``. rdflib's own default datatype inference for a
``Decimal`` value has the same gap (``Literal(Decimal(42))``
lexicalizes as ``"42"``, not ``"42.0"``) - the fractional-zero digit
only survives if it's already present in whatever value is handed to
``Decimal(...)``/``Literal(...)``, which these functions never do.

Idempotent and defensive, matching the established
``starlayer.shacl.validator`` patch idiom.""" ;
        rdfs:label "patch_decimal_result_lexical_form" ;
        ns2:calls ns26:_find_comp ;
        ns2:filePath "packages/starlayer/starlayer/graph/query/operator_patches.py" ;
        ns2:hasReturnValue ns26:patch_decimal_result_lexical_form.returns ;
        ns2:lineEnd 249 ;
        ns2:lineStart 192 ;
        ns2:signature "def patch_decimal_result_lexical_form() -> bool" .

    ns26:patch_decimal_result_lexical_form.returns a ns2:ReturnValue ;
        ns2:annotationText "bool" ;
        ns2:hasType ns5:builtins.bool .

    ns26:patch_integer_cast_from_numeric_and_boolean dcterms:identifier "starlayer.graph.query.operator_patches.patch_integer_cast_from_numeric_and_boolean" ;
        a ns2:Function ;
        rdfs:comment """Fix a confirmed rdflib bug: ``xsd:integer(x)`` casts through
``int(<lexical form>)``, so a cast from an ``xsd:decimal``, ``xsd:double``,
``xsd:float`` or ``xsd:boolean`` is an error (``xsd:integer(16.0934)``,
``xsd:integer(true)``) although SPARQL 1.1 §17.5 (via XPath casting) allows
each of these: a number is truncated toward zero, ``true`` is 1 and
``false`` is 0. ``NaN`` and the infinities stay errors. A string argument
is still cast from its lexical form, so ``xsd:integer("16.0934")``
remains an error, as it should.

Wraps rdflib's registered ``xsd:integer`` cast, handling only those source
types and deferring to the original for everything else. Idempotent and
defensive, like the other patches in this module.""" ;
        rdfs:label "patch_integer_cast_from_numeric_and_boolean" ;
        ns2:filePath "packages/starlayer/starlayer/graph/query/operator_patches.py" ;
        ns2:hasReturnValue ns26:patch_integer_cast_from_numeric_and_boolean.returns ;
        ns2:lineEnd 301 ;
        ns2:lineStart 255 ;
        ns2:signature "def patch_integer_cast_from_numeric_and_boolean() -> bool" .

    ns26:patch_integer_cast_from_numeric_and_boolean.returns a ns2:ReturnValue ;
        ns2:annotationText "bool" ;
        ns2:hasType ns5:builtins.bool .

    ns26:patch_multiplicative_expression_type_promotion dcterms:identifier "starlayer.graph.query.operator_patches.patch_multiplicative_expression_type_promotion" ;
        a ns2:Function ;
        rdfs:comment """Fix a confirmed rdflib bug: ``MultiplicativeExpression`` (the ``*``/
``/`` operators) never applies SPARQL 1.1's numeric type-promotion rules
the way ``AdditiveExpression`` (``+``/``-``) already does - it always
computes via ``Decimal`` and returns ``Literal(res)`` with no explicit
``datatype=``, so rdflib infers ``xsd:decimal`` from the Python
``Decimal`` type regardless of the operands' actual datatypes. Per
SPARQL 1.1's op:numeric-multiply, ``xsd:integer * xsd:integer`` must
stay ``xsd:integer`` - stock rdflib instead returns
``"42"^^xsd:decimal`` for ``6 * 7``, not ``"42"^^xsd:integer``.

Division is different: op:numeric-divide always promotes to at least
``xsd:decimal`` even for two integers (this part of rdflib's behavior
is already correct) - but the whole-number *lexical form* it produces
for that case is separately broken (see
``patch_decimal_result_lexical_form`` below) and is also fixed here,
since both live in the same function.

Idempotent and defensive, matching the established
``starlayer.shacl.validator`` patch idiom - returns ``False`` without
raising if rdflib's internals don't match what this shim expects.""" ;
        rdfs:label "patch_multiplicative_expression_type_promotion" ;
        ns2:filePath "packages/starlayer/starlayer/graph/query/operator_patches.py" ;
        ns2:hasReturnValue ns26:patch_multiplicative_expression_type_promotion.returns ;
        ns2:lineEnd 186 ;
        ns2:lineStart 115 ;
        ns2:signature "def patch_multiplicative_expression_type_promotion() -> bool" .

    ns26:patch_multiplicative_expression_type_promotion.returns a ns2:ReturnValue ;
        ns2:annotationText "bool" ;
        ns2:hasType ns5:builtins.bool .

    ns26:patch_sameterm_simple_literal_is_xsd_string dcterms:identifier "starlayer.graph.query.operator_patches.patch_sameterm_simple_literal_is_xsd_string" ;
        a ns2:Function ;
        rdfs:comment """Fix a confirmed rdflib bug: ``sameTerm("foo", "foo"^^xsd:string)`` is
false because rdflib compares ``Literal("foo") == Literal("foo",
datatype=XSD.string)`` as different terms, though RDF Concepts defines a
simple literal as shorthand for the ``xsd:string`` literal.

Fixes ``sameTerm()`` only. Matching a triple pattern against stored data
still distinguishes the two forms, because the store compares them as
different terms; correcting that means changing ``Literal`` itself.
Idempotent and defensive, like the other patches in this module.""" ;
        rdfs:label "patch_sameterm_simple_literal_is_xsd_string" ;
        ns2:calls ns26:_find_comp ;
        ns2:filePath "packages/starlayer/starlayer/graph/query/operator_patches.py" ;
        ns2:hasReturnValue ns26:patch_sameterm_simple_literal_is_xsd_string.returns ;
        ns2:lineEnd 406 ;
        ns2:lineStart 373 ;
        ns2:signature "def patch_sameterm_simple_literal_is_xsd_string() -> bool" .

    ns26:patch_sameterm_simple_literal_is_xsd_string.returns a ns2:ReturnValue ;
        ns2:annotationText "bool" ;
        ns2:hasType ns5:builtins.bool .

    ns26:patch_strlang_rejects_empty_language_tag dcterms:identifier "starlayer.graph.query.operator_patches.patch_strlang_rejects_empty_language_tag" ;
        a ns2:Function ;
        rdfs:comment """Fix a confirmed rdflib bug: ``STRLANG("a", "")`` returns the plain
string ``"a"`` (an empty ``lang=`` is treated as no language), but an empty
language tag is not a valid tag, so the call is an error and the result
unbound (SPARQL 1.2 Query, ``STRLANG``).

Wraps rdflib's ``Builtin_STRLANG`` evaluation function and raises
``SPARQLError`` for an empty tag; everything else is delegated unchanged.
Idempotent and defensive, like the other patches in this module.""" ;
        rdfs:label "patch_strlang_rejects_empty_language_tag" ;
        ns2:calls ns26:_find_comp ;
        ns2:filePath "packages/starlayer/starlayer/graph/query/operator_patches.py" ;
        ns2:hasReturnValue ns26:patch_strlang_rejects_empty_language_tag.returns ;
        ns2:lineEnd 347 ;
        ns2:lineStart 307 ;
        ns2:signature "def patch_strlang_rejects_empty_language_tag() -> bool" .

    ns26:patch_strlang_rejects_empty_language_tag.returns a ns2:ReturnValue ;
        ns2:annotationText "bool" ;
        ns2:hasType ns5:builtins.bool .

    ns26:patch_triple_terms_are_not_iris dcterms:identifier "starlayer.graph.query.operator_patches.patch_triple_terms_are_not_iris" ;
        a ns2:Function ;
        rdfs:comment """Fix a leak of the internal triple-term encoding: on the rdf-1.1 backend a triple term is a ``tt:`` IRI, so
``isIRI(?t)`` was true and ``STR(?t)`` returned the internal IRI text. The term kinds are disjoint in SPARQL 1.2
(17.4.2.3: ``isIRI`` is true only for an IRI) and ``STR`` applies to IRIs and literals only, so ``isIRI`` is false and
``STR`` an error for a triple term, as in Oxigraph (GitHub issue #74). ``STR`` of a blank node is an error too (rdflib
returns the label; the native backends already give an error; GitHub issue #75).

Wraps rdflib's ``Builtin_isIRI`` and ``Builtin_STR`` evaluation functions; idempotent and defensive like the others here.""" ;
        rdfs:label "patch_triple_terms_are_not_iris" ;
        ns2:calls ns26:_find_comp ;
        ns2:filePath "packages/starlayer/starlayer/graph/query/operator_patches.py" ;
        ns2:hasReturnValue ns26:patch_triple_terms_are_not_iris.returns ;
        ns2:lineEnd 464 ;
        ns2:lineStart 420 ;
        ns2:signature "def patch_triple_terms_are_not_iris() -> bool" .

    ns26:patch_triple_terms_are_not_iris.returns a ns2:ReturnValue ;
        ns2:annotationText "bool" ;
        ns2:hasType ns5:builtins.bool .

