GRAPH <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/blob/main/packages/starlayer/starlayer/graph/query/update_patches.py> {
    ns63:update_patches.py dcterms:identifier "starlayer.graph.query.update_patches" ;
        a ns2:Module ;
        rdfs:comment """Monkeypatches for rdflib's SPARQL Update evaluation of graph management
operations on a ``Dataset`` (``rdflib.plugins.sparql.update``).

rdflib's update code mixes up "the default graph" with ``ctx.graph``, which is
the union of every graph when the dataset has ``default_union`` set (the
setting ``StarLayerDataset`` passes on so a ``GRAPH``-less ``WHERE`` sees all
the data). The graph management operations must act on the true default
graph (SPARQL 1.1 Update 3.2), so ``CLEAR DEFAULT`` wiped the whole dataset,
``ADD``/``COPY``/``MOVE`` involving ``DEFAULT`` crashed or lost data,
``CREATE`` always raised, ``DELETE WHERE { GRAPH ?g {...} }`` deleted nothing
and ``USING``/``USING NAMED`` tried to fetch the graph over the network
(GitHub issue #78). The bugs are in ``docs/upstream-issues/rdflib-upstream-issues.md``.

The data operations are patched too (GitHub issue #135): ``DELETE DATA``,
``DELETE WHERE`` and ``DELETE { }`` removed the triple from every graph of the
dataset (``ctx.graph`` is the dataset, and ``Dataset.remove`` removes from all
contexts), ``USING <g>`` made the delete template reach ``g``, ``USING NAMED``
restricted nothing, template triples that are not valid RDF were inserted, and
a missing graph was no error for ``CLEAR``/``DROP``/``ADD``/``COPY``/``MOVE``.

Each patch is idempotent, with a sentinel attribute, like the others in this
package.""" ;
        rdfs:label "update_patches" ;
        ns2:declares ns73:_dataset, ns73:_eval_create, ns73:_copy_into, ns73:_eval_drop, ns73:_graph_or_default, ns73:_require_graph, ns73:_eval_move, ns73:_remove_graph, ns73:patch_update_graph_management, ns73:_graph_exists, ns73:_graph_solutions, ns73:_eval_clear, ns73:_eval_delete_data, ns73:_graph_name, ns73:_default_graph, ns73:_target_graph, ns73:_using_where_context, ns73:_eval_insert_data, ns73:_is_valid_triple, ns73:_eval_copy, ns73:_eval_delete_where, ns73:_eval_add, ns73:_valid_triples, ns73:_named_graphs, ns73:_empty, ns73:_existing_graph, ns73:_eval_modify, ns73:_graphs ;
        ns2:filePath "packages/starlayer/starlayer/graph/query/update_patches.py" ;
        ns2:importsModule ns5:__future__, ns5:rdflib.plugins.sparql.evalutils, ns5:rdflib.term, ns5:rdflib.plugins.sparql.evaluate, ns5:rdflib .

    ns73:_copy_into dcterms:identifier "starlayer.graph.query.update_patches._copy_into" ;
        a ns2:Function ;
        rdfs:label "_copy_into" ;
        ns2:filePath "packages/starlayer/starlayer/graph/query/update_patches.py" ;
        ns2:hasParameter ns73:_copy_into.param.dst, ns73:_copy_into.param.src ;
