GRAPH <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/blob/main/packages/starlayer/starlayer/graph/serializers/turtle12.py> {
    ns74:turtle12.py dcterms:identifier "starlayer.graph.serializers.turtle12" ;
        a ns2:Module ;
        rdfs:comment """starlayer.graph.serializers.turtle12

Serialize a StarLayerGraph (or a raw rdflib.Graph with the SL internal
encoding) to Turtle 1.2 text, writing triple terms as <<( s p o )>>.

Entry point: serialize_turtle12(graph) -> str

Approach: walk sg.triples() directly — which already returns TripleTerm objects
and filters encoding triples — rather than post-processing rdflib's Turtle output.
This avoids the inline-bnode problem (rdflib collapses bnodes with no outgoing
triples to `[ ]`, losing their ID).""" ;
        rdfs:label "turtle12" ;
        ns2:declares ns43:WriterNamespaces, ns43:_tt_to_reif_str, ns43:_demote_unreachable_inline, ns43:_writer_namespaces, ns43:_pred_to_ttl, ns43:_blank_nodes_in_triple_terms, ns43:_valid_qname, ns43:_node_to_ttl, ns43:_graph_has_dirlangstring, ns43:render_turtle12, ns43:serialize_longturtle12, ns43:_graph_has_triple_term, ns43:_sort_key, ns43:_tt_to_str, ns43:serialize_turtle12, ns43:iter_lines_outside_strings, ns43:_fmt, ns43:_build_fold_map, ns43:_compute_list_heads ;
        ns2:filePath "packages/starlayer/starlayer/graph/serializers/turtle12.py" ;
        ns2:importsModule ns5:urllib.parse, ns5:rdflib, ns5:collections, ns5:re .

    ns43:WriterNamespaces dcterms:identifier "starlayer.graph.serializers.turtle12.WriterNamespaces" ;
        a ns2:Class ;
        rdfs:comment """The prefix bindings a Turtle/TriG writer may use, taken from a graph's namespace manager.

The writers used to ask the namespace manager for every name, which (a) hands out a prefix that is not a valid PN_PREFIX
(``a.``, ``a:b``, ``1x``, ``_``, which silently turns IRIs into blank nodes) and (b) answers from a cache that is not cleared
when a prefix is rebound, so a renamed prefix came out with its OLD name and no ``@prefix`` line (GitHub issues #132, #133).
Here a binding whose prefix is not valid is renamed ``pfxN`` (a free number; not ``nsN``, which rdflib itself hands out for
a namespace it has no prefix for), a name is found among the CURRENT bindings
(the longest namespace whose remainder is a valid local name), and only when none fits is the manager asked to make
a new prefix. ``base``, when given, makes ``iri_ref()`` write IRIs under it relative (and the writer emits ``@base``).""" ;
        rdfs:label "WriterNamespaces" ;
        ns2:declares ns43:WriterNamespaces.iri_ref, ns43:WriterNamespaces._lookup, ns43:WriterNamespaces._rebuild, ns43:WriterNamespaces.namespaces, ns43:WriterNamespaces.__init__, ns43:WriterNamespaces.qname ;
