    ns86:_build_string_component.StringConstraintComponent dcterms:identifier "starlayer.shacl.native_components._build_string_component.StringConstraintComponent" ;
        a ns2:Class ;
        rdfs:comment """Shadows a pySHACL string constraint (``sh:pattern``,
``sh:minLength``, ``sh:maxLength``): an encoded triple term violates
it, and an invalid ``sh:pattern`` raises ``ConstraintLoadError`` naming
the shape instead of a raw ``re.error`` (GitHub issue #94).

``sh:pattern`` is SPARQL ``REGEX`` (XPath syntax). pySHACL compiles it with Python's ``re``, which rejects ``\\p{L}``,
``\\i``/``\\c`` and reads ``[a-z-[aeiou]]`` as a different class; ``xpath_regex`` translates those (a pattern without
them is compiled untouched), and a pattern it cannot translate raises ``ConstraintLoadError`` naming the feature.""" ;
        rdfs:label "StringConstraintComponent" ;
        rdfs:subClassOf ns5:original ;
        ns2:declares ns86:_build_string_component.StringConstraintComponent.evaluate, ns86:_build_string_component.StringConstraintComponent.__init__ ;
