GRAPH <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/blob/main/packages/starlayer/starlayer/shacl/shacl_profiling.py> {
    ns76:shacl_profiling.py dcterms:identifier "starlayer.shacl.shacl_profiling" ;
        a ns2:Module ;
        rdfs:comment """The public namespace for SHACL 1.2 Profiling - `from starlayer.shacl
import shacl_profiling` then `shacl_profiling.declared_conformance_profile`/
`shacl_profiling.derive_conforms_to`.

A thin re-export of `profiling.py`'s own two functions - the real SHACL 1.2
Profiling spec (https://www.w3.org/TR/shacl12-profiling/) implementation.
Not flattened into `starlayer.shacl`'s own top-level namespace, mirroring
`starlayer.sparql.srl`/`sqe`'s own precedent of a dedicated submodule per
spec document.

For the unrelated validator-option-preset concept (the `"validation"`/
`"rules"`/`"debug"` presets selected via `validate(mode=...)`), see
`starlayer.shacl.validation_modes` instead - that concept has nothing to
do with this SHACL document despite the shared English word "profile.\"""" ;
        rdfs:label "shacl_profiling" ;
        ns2:filePath "packages/starlayer/starlayer/shacl/shacl_profiling.py" ;
        ns2:importsModule ns5:__future__ .

    ns5:__future__ a ns2:ExternalModule .
}

GRAPH <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/blob/main/packages/starlayer/starlayer/shacl/shape_types.py> {
    ns76:shape_types.py dcterms:identifier "starlayer.shacl.shape_types" ;
        a ns2:Module ;
        rdfs:comment """``infer_types()`` - the types a shapes graph's structure entails (GitHub issues #24, #27, #28).

SHACL 1.2 Core leaves much of a shape's typing to the engine: a shape need not say ``rdf:type sh:NodeShape`` (3.2) or
``sh:PropertyShape`` (3.3), and 3.1 makes a node a shape through its targets, its constraint parameters, being the value of
a shape-valued parameter, or being on the list that is the value of ``sh:and``/``sh:or``/``sh:xone``. A tool that lists the
entities of a shapes file by type needs those triples.

Two sources, both from the registry:

1. **The SHACL vocabulary** (``shacl_vocabulary``): RDFS entailment over the shapes graph plus the vocabulary's
   ``rdfs:domain``/``rdfs:range`` types things that are not shapes (the value of ``sh:group`` is a ``sh:PropertyGroup``, the
   subject of ``sh:validator`` a ``sh:ConstraintComponent``). The vocabulary's domain for ``sh:name`` and ``sh:description``
   is ``sh:Shape``, but a property group has them too, so those two are left out of the entailment.
2. **The rules** (``shacl_shacl_rules``): SHACL rules for what RDFS cannot say (a list walk, an absent ``sh:path``), and the node
   expressions under ``sh:values``/``sh:defaultValue``/``sh:expression`` (typed ``sh:NodeExpression``, at any nesting depth, with the cells
   of their argument lists typed ``rdf:List``) so that every node there has a shape that targets it (GitHub issue #22).

The result holds only new ``rdf:type`` triples, in the ``sh:`` namespace; it never contains what the shapes graph already
says, and the shapes graph is not changed.""" ;
        rdfs:label "shape_types" ;
        ns2:declares ns98:infer_types, ns98:_copy, ns98:_is_vocabulary_term ;
        ns2:filePath "packages/starlayer/starlayer/shacl/shape_types.py" ;
        ns2:importsModule ns5:rdflib, ns5:__future__, ns5:typing .

    ns98:_copy dcterms:identifier "starlayer.shacl.shape_types._copy" ;
        a ns2:Function ;
        rdfs:label "_copy" ;
        ns2:filePath "packages/starlayer/starlayer/shacl/shape_types.py" ;
        ns2:hasParameter ns98:_copy.param.graph ;
        ns2:hasReturnValue ns98:_copy.returns ;
        ns2:instantiates ns32:StarLayerGraph ;
        ns2:isPrivate true ;
        ns2:lineEnd 49 ;
        ns2:lineStart 43 ;
        ns2:signature "def _copy(graph: Any) -> StarLayerGraph" .

    ns98:_copy.param.graph a ns2:Parameter ;
