GRAPH <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/blob/main/packages/starlayer/starlayer/shacl/xpath_regex.py> {
    ns76:xpath_regex.py dcterms:identifier "starlayer.shacl.xpath_regex" ;
        a ns2:Module ;
        rdfs:comment """Translate the XPath/XSD regular-expression syntax of ``sh:pattern`` to Python's ``re`` (GitHub issue #94).

``sh:pattern`` is SPARQL ``REGEX``, whose syntax is XPath ``fn:matches`` (XSD 1.0 Appendix F plus XPath additions). Python's
``re`` shares most of it. What it lacks is translated here:

* ``\\p{L}``, ``\\p{Lu}``, ``\\P{Nd}`` (general categories, from ``unicodedata``) and ``\\p{IsBasicLatin}`` (block names, a
  table of the common XSD blocks);
* ``\\i``, ``\\I``, ``\\c``, ``\\C`` (XML name start character / name character and their complements);
* character class subtraction ``[a-z-[aeiou]]``, which Python compiles to a *different* class without an error.

A pattern that uses none of these is returned unchanged (:func:`needs_translation` is false), so the translation can never alter
a pattern that already works. Anything it cannot translate (an unknown category or block name, a malformed escape) raises
``ValueError`` with a message naming the feature.""" ;
        rdfs:label "xpath_regex" ;
        ns2:declares ns89:_translate_class, ns89:_normalise, ns89:_ranges_text, ns89:needs_translation, ns89:_read_property_name, ns89:_categories, ns89:xpath_regex_to_python, ns89:_complement, ns89:_property_ranges, ns89:_escape_ranges ;
        ns2:filePath "packages/starlayer/starlayer/shacl/xpath_regex.py" ;
        ns2:importsModule ns5:sys, ns5:re, ns5:__future__, ns5:unicodedata .

    ns89:_categories dcterms:identifier "starlayer.shacl.xpath_regex._categories" ;
