GRAPH <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/blob/main/packages/starlayer/starlayer/sparql/expr_families.py> {
    ns102:expr_families.py dcterms:identifier "starlayer.sparql.expr_families" ;
        a ns2:Module ;
        rdfs:comment """``_EXPR_NODE_FAMILY``: name -> argument-signature family, for every one
of rdflib's 63 expression builtins. Shared, dependency-free source of truth (lives here, not inside ``salg/``: ``sqe:``, ``srl:`` and the shared
encoder all use it, and none of them should import ``salg``)
for ``expr_validation.py`` (generates the per-builtin SHACL shapes from it)
and ``salg/sparql_ontology.py`` (generates per-builtin ``rdfs:subClassOf``
declarations from it) — lives in its own module, not either of those,
specifically so ``sparql_ontology.py`` never needs ``pyshacl`` (a
``sparql_shapes.py``-only dependency) just to read this table.

``from_rdf._discover_expr_evalfns()`` is the live source of truth for the
*name list* (rebuilt by walking rdflib's own pyparsing grammar, so it can't
drift out of sync with whatever rdflib version is installed); the family for
each name was confirmed by building a real query exercising it and
inspecting the decoded algebra node's own keys directly — not guessed from
the name, since that's genuinely unreliable here (e.g. ``Builtin_REPLACE``'s
keys are ``arg``/``pattern``/``replacement``/``flags``, not
``arg1``..``arg4``; ``Builtin_BNODE``'s sole argument is optional unlike
every other one-arg builtin).""" ;
        rdfs:label "expr_families" ;
        ns2:filePath "packages/starlayer/starlayer/sparql/expr_families.py" ;
        ns2:importsModule ns5:__future__ .

    ns5:__future__ a ns2:ExternalModule .
}

GRAPH <https://github.com/hidden-graph/starlayer/blob/main/packages/starlayer/starlayer/sparql/expr_text.py> {
    ns102:expr_text.py dcterms:identifier "starlayer.sparql.expr_text" ;
        a ns2:Module ;
        rdfs:comment """Render a SPARQL expression tree (rdflib algebra ``Expr``/``CompValue``) back to text.

rdflib's ``translateAlgebra`` loses information on expressions: it drops the parentheses of arithmetic, drops the flags
argument of ``REGEX`` and ``REPLACE``, and prints ``{UnaryMinus}``, ``{Function}`` or ``{Builtin_isTRIPLE}`` placeholders for
node kinds it does not know (GitHub issue #80). This renderer walks the tree itself. It accepts both the raw parse tree (a
chain of single-child ``ConditionalOrExpression`` ... ``MultiplicativeExpression`` wrappers) and a simplified one, and
parenthesises every operator node that is an operand of another operator, so the text means what the tree means whatever the
precedence rules say.

Raises ``NotImplementedError`` for a node kind it does not handle (``EXISTS`` and the aggregates), so a caller can fall back.""" ;
        rdfs:label "expr_text" ;
        ns2:declares ns110:_render, ns110:_args, ns110:_text, ns110:_operand, ns110:render_expression, ns110:_render_triple_term ;
        ns2:filePath "packages/starlayer/starlayer/sparql/expr_text.py" ;
        ns2:importsModule ns5:rdflib.plugins.sparql.parserutils, ns5:__future__, ns5:rdflib .

